There's no reason to have the only stash in Minetown. An altar is not
required. Nor is there an upper limit to the number of stashes you can
have.

>                Now from the Sokoban to the minetown is a long way and as 
> the player told his character didn't have any sack or BoH, ergo he had 
> to lug everything in the open inventory.

Make an improvised stash on the branch to Soko. Whenever you get burdened
in or around Soko, go there and stash surplus stuff. When you find the
time, you can move the stashes and merge them on another level as you get
deeper. 

In my opinion, a stash in the mines doesn't make much sense. Sure, you'll
pick up a lot of heavy armor that you want to BUC-test, but there's no need
to keep the surplus. Just make a stash in the main dungeon for surplus
potions, books, scrolls and the like and make your mines excursions from
there.

